{"shortDescription":"The Japanese yen appreciated past 160 per dollar on Monday but remained near one-month lows as the dollar strengthened following hawkish remarks from Federal Reserve Chair Kevin Warsh that boosted expectations for a US rate hike in September.Markets are now pricing in around a 57% chance that the F…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["The Japanese yen appreciated past 160 per dollar on Monday but remained near one-month lows as the dollar strengthened following hawkish remarks from Federal Reserve Chair Kevin Warsh that boosted expectations for a US rate hike in September."]},{"type":"p","children":["Markets are now pricing in around a 57% chance that the Fed will raise rates by 25 basis points next month, up sharply from about 40% a week ago."]},{"type":"p","children":["Traders are also betting on a potential Bank of Japan rate increase in September amid concerns over yen weakness and import-driven inflation."]},{"type":"p","children":["The yen has retraced more than half of its gains following the joint Japan-US currency market intervention in late July, with persistent structural weakness continuing to weigh on the currency."]},{"type":"p","children":["The yen remained under pressure from wide interest rate differentials, growing fiscal concerns in Japan and elevated oil prices linked to the Middle East conflict."]}]},"language":"en","tags":[{"title":"Forex","args":[{"id":"category","value":"forex"}]},{"title":"Trading Economics","args":[{"id":"provider","value":"trading-economics"}]}],"id":"te_news:579327:0","title":"Yen Languishes Near 1-Month Low","published":1788141541,"urgency":2,"link":"https://tradingeconomics.com/japan/currency","permission":"preview","relatedSymbols":[{"symbol":"FX:USDJPY","currency-logoid":"country/JP","base-currency-logoid":"country/US","logo":{"style":"pair","logoid":"country/US","logoid2":"country/JP"}},{"symbol":"FTMO_OANDA:USDJPY.SIM","currency-logoid":"country/JP","base-curren